# Mental Health Signal

### Machine Learning-Based Student Mental Health Prediction

Mental Health Signal is a machine learning application designed to predict a student's mental health score based on academic, lifestyle, stress, sleep, physical activity, and social media usage factors.

The project combines a trained Scikit-learn pipeline with a FastAPI backend and provides a REST API for real-time predictions.

---

## Overview

Mental health among students can be influenced by a combination of academic pressure, lifestyle habits, and digital behavior.

This project explores these factors and uses a machine learning model to estimate a student's mental health score from user-provided information.

The application includes:

- A trained machine learning pipeline
- FastAPI REST API
- Pydantic-based input validation
- Interactive API documentation
- Web-based frontend
- Cloud deployment using Render

---

## Features

- Predicts a student's mental health score
- Validates API input using Pydantic
- Handles categorical and numerical features
- Uses a serialized Scikit-learn pipeline
- Provides RESTful prediction endpoints
- Interactive Swagger API documentation
- CORS-enabled frontend integration
- Deployed and accessible through Render

---

## Technology Stack

| Category | Technology |
|---|---|
| Language | Python |
| Machine Learning | Scikit-learn |
| Data Processing | Pandas, NumPy |
| API Framework | FastAPI |
| Validation | Pydantic |
| Model Serialization | Joblib |
| Frontend | HTML, CSS, JavaScript |
| Version Control | Git, GitHub |
| Deployment | Render |

